### Summary

In this program, a **Max Heap** is implemented using Python. A Max Heap is a complete binary tree in which the parent node is always greater than or equal to its child nodes. The program takes elements from the user, inserts them into the Max Heap, displays the heap, finds the maximum element, and deletes the maximum element.

The time complexity for inserting one element and deleting the maximum element is **O(log n)**. When `n` elements are inserted one by one, the overall time complexity is **O(n log n)**. The space complexity of the Max Heap is **O(n)**.

### Conclusion

The Max Heap was successfully implemented using Python with user input. The program demonstrates important heap operations such as **insertion, finding the maximum element, and deletion**. It also shows the time and space complexity of the algorithm. Max Heap is useful in applications such as **priority queues, heap sort, and scheduling algorithms**.
